{
 "what": "The Hamilton costumes for midtown.html's automatic actors (THE COSTUMES; docs/hamilton-costumes-format.md). `costumes`: each look, its garments and their colours. `plot`: each body (tools/hamilton-cast.json ids) and its looks in the show's order, each worn from the start of a track (album ids) - changed into off stage, at the moment the body last went off before it, unless `onstage`.",
 "design": "Paul Tazewell, the Original Broadway production (Richard Rodgers Theatre). A parchment base for the company with character added on top; no wigs but King George's; boots in the war, stockings and shoes for the statesmen; almost everyone back in parchment for the finale.",
 "sourcing": "Each look's `source`: S = written down (Tazewell's notes, the Smithsonian's record of the green suit, reviews of the film); I = read off the film or inferred. Most colours and many song boundaries are I - check them against the film.",
